@startuml controlled-restart
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Controlled restart: park, forced stop, exit, resume bridge, report

actor "Operator" as OP $PERSON
participant "Daemon\n(session host)" as D $SERVICE
participant "Orchestrator\nsessions" as S $AGENT
participant "Board kernel" as K $SERVICE
database "Board" as B $COMMITTED
participant "OS service manager\n(launchd, systemd)" as SV $PRIVATE
participant "Resume bridge\n(login shell)" as RB $SERVICE

== Close and park ==
OP -> D: controlled restart
D -> D: close admission\n(durable ordinary closure, survives exit;\nany held update lock stays set)
D -> D: serialize starts, wakes, retries,\nconsumer-starting probes\nagainst both fences
D -> S: park broadcast
S -> B: park note per session
D -> K: request goal revision\nwith handoff_ref
K -> B: commit goal revision
K --> D: committed revision\n(observed ready signal)
D -> D: drain turns, approvals,\nlandings, integrates, pushes,\nledger latches
alt all parked before the bound
  D -> D: confirm every stop
else bound reached
  D -> S: forced resumable stops
  D -> D: record forced stops and\nsnapshot fallbacks distinctly
end
break unresolved stops or\nunsettled safe points
  D -> D: retain ordinary closure\nfor recovery
  D --> OP: recovery report\n(no restore path)
end

== Exit and restart ==
note over D
  reached only on confirmed consumer exit
  and settled safe points
  (incl. detached consumers, Muse latches)
end note
D -> D: exit (ordinary closure stays for recovery\nuntil reconciliation completes;\nupdate lock untouched)
SV -> D: start the replacement
D -> D: reconcile closure\nand park records
break ordinary closure unresolved
  D -> D: retain ordinary closure\nfor recovery
  D --> OP: recovery report\n(no restore path)
end
D -> D: ordinary closure ends\n(a held update lock stays set)

== Resume bridge ==
RB -> RB: wait for harness auth readiness\nwithin the bound\n(launch nothing while logged out)
break auth not ready within the bound
  D -> D: park with reason;\nretain goal, hold queued work\nuntil readiness
  D --> OP: report every session\n+ host-health section
end
RB -> D: curator run <env> --hosted resume <SES>\n(plan recomposed, no stored env)
opt update lock set
  OP -> D: clear the update lock\n(only after recovery/update\nconditions hold)
end
break update lock still set
  D -> D: hold automatic restore;\nsessions stay parked
  D --> OP: report every session\n+ host-health section\n(no restored consumer)
end
D -> D: version gate: probes,\nknown-bad check, last-known-good
D -> D: preserve explicit stops\nas skipped/stopped outcomes
D -> S: resume eligible sessions\nnatively or start fresh\nfrom goal + park note\n(children resume under root)
opt RC requested
  D -> D: wait within the bound\nfor the requested RC registration
  break registration not observed\nwithin the bound
    D -> D: park with reason;\nretain goal, hold queued work\nuntil readiness
    D --> OP: report every session\n+ host-health section
  end
end
D --> OP: report every session\n+ host-health section

note over OP, SV
  A forced stop is not an emergency stop.
  keeper estop stays a separate command.
end note

caption Sources: Architecture v1 §A7; PR #8 (branch amend/version-gate-update-window); spec §8, §11, §14
@enduml
